      "summary": "Khiva: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 2: Khiva: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Khiva - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/khiva-character.jpg)\n\nSurrounded by the harsh expanse of the Karakum and Kyzylkum deserts, Khiva's walled inner citadel of Itchan Kala is the most complete medieval city in Central Asia. A circuit of ten-meter-high, undulating sun-baked mud-brick walls with rounded bastions protects a compact labyrinth of fifty historic monuments and hundreds of clay-plastered dwellings.\n\n![Geographic location of Khiva in Uzbekistan](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/khiva-map.png)\n\nThe city is anchored by the dazzling Kalta Minor minaret, an unfinished cylindrical tower completely encrusted in gleaming turquoise, cobalt, and white glazed majolica tiles. Inside the Juma Mosque, a tranquil forest of two hundred and eighteen intricately carved elm-wood pillars supports the timber ceiling, while the terracotta watchtowers of the Kuhna Ark offer breathtaking views of desert sunsets turning clay domes into molten gold."
