      "summary": "Isfahan: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 3: Isfahan: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Isfahan - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/isfahan-character.jpg)\n\nCelebrated in Persian poetry with the famous proverb 'Isfahan is half the world', this oasis capital represents the zenith of Islamic architecture under Shah Abbas I. At its core lies the monumental Naqsh-e Jahan Square, one of the largest public plazas in the world, framed by double-tiered arched arcades that once hosted polo matches and royal parades.\n\n![Geographic location of Isfahan in Iran](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/isfahan-map.png)\n\nAt the southern end stands the breathtaking Shah Mosque, an ocean of seven-colored mosaic tiles and spiraling calligraphy that seems to float beneath a colossal turquoise dome. Along the Zayandeh River, historic multi-arched stone bridges like the Si-o-se-pol and Khaju Bridge feature arched pavilions where locals gather to sing traditional Persian melodies in the evening coolness."
