      "summary": "Shiraz: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 4: Shiraz: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Shiraz - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/shiraz-character.jpg)\n\nNestled in a fertile mountain valley of southwest Iran, Shiraz is celebrated as the cultural soul of Persia, famed for its poetry, wine, and aromatic citrus gardens. The city honors legendary medieval poets Hafez and Saadi with open-air garden mausoleums where pilgrims read verse aloud beside bubbling fountains and cypress trees.\n\n![Geographic location of Shiraz in Iran](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/shiraz-map.png)\n\nThe city's most mesmerizing jewel is the nineteenth-century Nasir al-Mulk Mosque (the Pink Mosque), where morning sunlight streams through kaleidoscopic stained-glass windows, projecting a dazzling rainbow tapestry of crimson, turquoise, and gold across hand-woven Persian carpets. Nearby, the walled Eram Garden exemplifies the classical Persian paradise garden layout with waterways flowing through fragrant orange groves."
