      "content": "### Chapter 6: Kashan: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Kashan - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/kashan-character.jpg)\n\nLocated on the northern edge of the great Iranian desert, Kashan is an oasis jewel famed for its rosewater distilleries, hand-knotted silk carpets, and splendid Qajar-era residential architecture. Following devastating eighteenth-century earthquakes, wealthy merchants constructed sprawling mud-brick mansions featuring multi-tiered sunken courtyards, subterranean reservoirs, and intricate mirrored stucco ceilings.\n\n![Geographic location of Kashan in Iran](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/kashan-map.png)\n\nThe Tabatabaei and Borujerdi houses showcase exquisite bas-relief plasterwork depicting birds and floral motifs, alongside stained-glass windcatcher rooms designed for desert cooling. On the edge of town, the UNESCO-listed Fin Garden is the oldest surviving Persian garden, where mountain spring water gushes through turquoise stone canals beneath majestic cypress trees planted centuries ago."
