      "summary": "Konya: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 7: Konya: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Konya - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/konya-character.jpg)\n\nSet upon the vast Anatolian high plateau, Konya was the proud capital of the Seljuk Sultanate of Rum and remains the spiritual capital of Sufi mysticism. The heart of the city is the Mevlana Museum, crowned by an iconic ribbed turquoise dome, which houses the tomb of the legendary mystic poet and philosopher Jalal al-Din Rumi.\n\n![Geographic location of Konya in Turkey](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/konya-map.png)\n\nHere, the Mevlevi Order of Whirling Dervishes practice their mesmerizing sema ritual, spinning in flowing white robes to traditional reed flute music in a meditative pursuit of divine unity. Splendid Seljuk stone monuments, such as the Karatay Madrasah and the Ince Minareli Madrasah with its elaborately carved stone portal, reflect an era of intense intellectual and spiritual golden age."
