      "summary": "Petra: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 8: Petra: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Petra - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/petra-character.jpg)\n\nHidden deep within the rugged desert canyons of southwestern Jordan, Petra was the flourishing capital of the Nabataean kingdom over two thousand years ago. Entering via the Siq—a dark, serpentine canyon flanked by ninety-meter sandstone walls—leads to the breathtaking reveal of Al-Khazneh (the Treasury), an ornate forty-meter facade carved directly into the living rose-red rock.\n\n![Geographic location of Petra in Jordan](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/petra-map.png)\n\nBeyond the Treasury, an entire ancient city unfolds across the desert mountains: hundreds of rock-cut royal tombs with striated pink and gold sandstone, a massive amphitheater carved from a cliff face, and the colossal monastery of Ad Deir, reached by an eight-hundred-step climb through dramatic desert chasms overlooking the Wadi Araba."
