      "title": "AlUla: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "AlUla: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 9: AlUla: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![AlUla - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/alula-character.jpg)\n\nNestled in a fertile desert valley among dramatic golden sandstone massifs in northwest Saudi Arabia, AlUla was a crucial crossroads on the ancient incense and spice routes. The old mud-brick town of AlUla features nearly nine hundred interconnected adobe houses and stone watchtowers built against a sheer red-rock escarpment.\n\n![Geographic location of AlUla in Saudi Arabia](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/alula-map.png)\n\nJust north of the oasis lies Hegra (Mada'in Salih), Saudi Arabia's first UNESCO World Heritage site, featuring over one hundred monumental tombs carved into solitary sandstone monoliths rising from desert sands. Intricate eagle carvings, floral rosettes, and Nabataean inscriptions adorn the facades, glowing in deep copper and amber hues under the stark desert sun."
