      "summary": "Luxor: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 10: Luxor: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Luxor - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/luxor-character.jpg)\n\nBuilt upon the ancient site of Thebes—the glorious capital of Egypt's New Kingdom for over five hundred years—Luxor is an archaeological treasure house without equal. On the East Bank of the Nile, the colossal Karnak Temple complex features the Hypostyle Hall, an awe-inspiring stone forest of one hundred and thirty-four gigantic sandstone columns towering up to twenty-one meters high.\n\n![Geographic location of Luxor in Egypt](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/luxor-map.png)\n\nConnecting Karnak to the elegant Luxor Temple is the ancient Avenue of Sphinxes, a three-kilometer paved ceremonial path lined with hundreds of stone human- and ram-headed sphinxes. At twilight, illuminated temple pylons reflect in the slow-moving waters of the Nile, where traditional white-sailed feluccas drift past palm-fringed banks backed by the rugged limestone cliffs of the Theban Necropolis."
