      "title": "Siwa Oasis: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Siwa Oasis: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 12: Siwa Oasis: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Siwa Oasis - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/siwa-oasis-character.jpg)\n\nIsolated in the deep expanse of Egypt's Western Desert near the Libyan border, Siwa Oasis is an extraordinary Eden of three hundred thousand date palms, olive groves, and turquoise salt pools fed by natural desert springs. Dominating the oasis is the medieval fortress of Shali, an astonishing ancient mud citadel constructed from kershef—a unique local blend of salt, clay, and sand that hardens in the sun.\n\n![Geographic location of Siwa Oasis in Egypt](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/siwa-oasis-map.png)\n\nA short distance away stands the ruined Temple of the Oracle of Amun, visited in 331 BC by Alexander the Great to confirm his divine sonship. Visitors swim in the crystal-clear thermal waters of Cleopatra's Pool, where mineral springs bubble up among palm groves, while surrounding colossal dunes of the Great Sand Sea glow rose-gold under desert starlight."
