      "summary": "Marrakesh: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 13: Marrakesh: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Marrakesh - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/marrakesh-character.jpg)\n\nFounded in 1062 by the Almoravid dynasty at the foot of the snow-capped High Atlas Mountains, Marrakesh is Morocco's legendary Red City, encircled by nineteen kilometers of monumental pink-and-ochre pisé clay ramparts. The heart of the city is the Koutoubia Mosque, whose seventy-seven-meter stone minaret has guided desert caravans for nearly a thousand years.\n\n![Geographic location of Marrakesh in Morocco](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/marrakesh-map.png)\n\nBy day, the winding labyrinth of souks overflows with fragrant spices, hand-hammered brass lanterns, Berber carpets, and leather babouche slippers. At dusk, the vast plaza of Jemaa el-Fnaa transforms into a legendary open-air theater of snake charmers, storytellers, Gnawa musicians, and sizzling food stalls sending aromatic clouds of grilled meats and cumin into the warm desert evening."
