      "content": "### Chapter 15: Ghadames: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Ghadames - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/ghadames-character.jpg)\n\nLocated at the desert junction where the borders of Libya, Algeria, and Tunisia meet, Ghadames is acclaimed as the Pearl of the Sahara. The historic walled city is an architectural marvel of climate adaptation: entirely whitewashed mud-and-palm-trunk houses are interconnected by vaulted subterranean streets that remain pleasantly cool even in extreme desert heat.\n\n![Geographic location of Ghadames in Libya](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/ghadames-map.png)\n\nA unique social design feature is the rooftop level: open-air terraces atop the houses were historically reserved exclusively for women to socialize and travel across the city without descending to the street level. In the lush oasis gardens, ancient underground water channels (foggara) distribute mountain spring water to thousands of date palms and pomegranate orchards."
