      "title": "Shibam: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Shibam: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 16: Shibam: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Shibam - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/shibam-character.jpg)\n\nRising like an astonishing forest of stone from the arid valley floor of the Wadi Hadramaut, Shibam is renowned worldwide as the oldest skyscraper city on Earth. Nearly five hundred multi-story apartment towers—reaching up to eleven stories and thirty meters tall—are packed tightly within a fortified trapezoidal wall, constructed entirely of sun-baked mud bricks and straw.\n\n![Geographic location of Shibam in Yemen](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/shibam-map.png)\n\nTo protect the earthen walls from rare but torrential flash floods, upper stories and roof parapets are coated in gleaming white lime plaster. Intricately carved wooden lattice screens and heavy cedar-wood doors provide ventilation and privacy. At sunset, the vertical mud-brick facades glow in warm shades of amber and terracotta against the stark limestone desert plateau."
