      "summary": "Sana'a: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 17: Sana'a: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Sana'a - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/sanaa-character.jpg)\n\nSituated in a mountain basin at an elevation of twenty-two hundred meters, the Old City of Sana'a is one of the world's oldest continuously inhabited urban treasures, traditionally said to have been founded by Noah's son Shem. The cityscape is defined by thousands of tower houses up to eight stories high, built of dark basalt stone foundations and warm-brown fired brick.\n\n![Geographic location of Sana'a in Yemen](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/sanaa-map.png)\n\nThe upper floors are decorated with dazzling white gypsum tracery and stained-glass crescent windows called qamariyahs, which illuminate interior reception rooms (mafrajs) in vibrant hues. The ancient city wall, pierced by the monumental Bab al-Yaman gate, shelters bustling souks filled with frankincense, myrrh, silver dagger filigree (jambiyas), and rich Yemeni coffee."
