      "title": "Lalibela: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Lalibela: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 18: Lalibela: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Lalibela - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/lalibela-character.jpg)\n\nConceived in the twelfth century by King Gebre Mesqel Lalibela as a New Jerusalem following the Muslim conquest of the Holy Land, Lalibela is a sacred marvel of human devotion and engineering. Rather than being built up from the ground, eleven medieval Christian churches were chiseled directly downward into solid red volcanic scoria rock.\n\n![Geographic location of Lalibela in Ethiopia](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/lalibela-map.png)\n\nThe most iconic sanctuary is Bete Giyorgis (Church of Saint George), carved in the shape of a colossal Greek cross standing twelve meters deep in an excavated pit, connected by deep subterranean trenches and catacombs. White-robed Orthodox priests and hermits chant ancient Ge'ez liturgies to the rhythm of brass sistrums and wooden prayer sticks, keeping a thousand-year-old spiritual heritage alive."
