      "summary": "Harar: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 19: Harar: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Harar - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/harar-character.jpg)\n\nPerched atop an escarpment in eastern Ethiopia overlooking the Somali plains, Harar Jugol is celebrated as the fourth holiest city of Islam. Enclosed within thick sixteenth-century stone walls pierced by five historic gates, the city packs eighty-two mosques and over one hundred shrines into a tight labyrinth of three hundred and sixty-eight narrow alleys.\n\n![Geographic location of Harar in Ethiopia](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/harar-map.png)\n\nTraditional Harari townhouses (Gegar) feature whitewashed stone walls, elevated carpeted seating platforms (nadaba) decorated with enameled plates and woven baskets, and peaceful inner courtyards. In the evening, the legendary hyena men of Harar feed wild spotted hyenas by hand outside the city walls, an extraordinary ritual of coexistence passed down through centuries."
