      "summary": "Timbuktu: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 20: Timbuktu: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Timbuktu - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/timbuktu-character.jpg)\n\nResting at the southern edge of the Sahara Desert where the great camel routes met the waters of the Niger River, Timbuktu became synonymous in world lore with the ultimate distant mystery. During the golden age of the Mali and Songhai empires, the city flourished as a world-renowned center of Islamic learning, boasting twenty-five thousand scholars at the University of Sankore.\n\n![Geographic location of Timbuktu in Mali](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/timbuktu-map.png)\n\nThe city's architectural icons include the fourteenth-century Djinguereber Mosque, built of mud brick, timber beams, and limestone plaster, whose earthen minarets dominate the sandy streets. Deep within private family libraries, hundreds of thousands of illuminated medieval manuscripts on astronomy, mathematics, medicine, and law are preserved, testifying to West Africa's brilliant intellectual heritage."
