      "summary": "Jaisalmer: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 21: Jaisalmer: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Jaisalmer - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/jaisalmer-character.jpg)\n\nRising dramatically from the desolate yellow sands of the Thar Desert, Jaisalmer is India's Golden City. Crowned upon Trikuta Hill is the colossal Jaisalmer Fort (Sonar Qila), constructed of warm yellow sandstone without mortar in 1156, its ninety-nine rounded bastions glowing in incandescent gold under the desert sun.\n\n![Geographic location of Jaisalmer in India](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/jaisalmer-map.png)\n\nUnlike most forts, Jaisalmer is a living citadel where a quarter of the town's population resides inside the ramparts. The narrow cobblestone alleys are lined with havelis (mansions) like Patwon Ki Haveli, featuring stone-carved jharokha balconies so delicate they resemble lace woven from rock. Within the fort, seven intricately carved medieval Jain temples house thousands of ancient statues and sacred palm-leaf manuscripts."
