      "summary": "Jodhpur: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 4",
      "content": "### Chapter 22: Jodhpur: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Jodhpur - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/jodhpur-character.jpg)\n\nSpreading across the arid rocky plains at the threshold of the Thar Desert, Jodhpur is world-famous as the Blue City. At its heart, looming one hundred and twenty meters above on a sheer volcanic cliff, is the colossal Mehrangarh Fort—one of the most formidable defensive structures ever built, with red sandstone walls soaring up to thirty-six meters high.\n\n![Geographic location of Jodhpur in India](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-04/images/jodhpur-map.png)\n\nBelow the fort walls lies a mesmerizing labyrinth of cubical Brahmin houses painted in vivid shades of indigo blue to repel insects and keep interiors cool. From the fort ramparts lined with historic cannons, the panorama of blue rooftops stretching toward the desert horizon under the shadow of the clock tower bazaar is one of Rajasthan's most unforgettable vistas."
